00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.300
The single source leaves open how quickly regulators will approve the service.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.160
The agreement covers the airlines fleet operating from Vietnam.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:52.440
To really understand how trade truces are kept in place, consider the quiet technical talks

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:58.420
between mid-level officials who align tariff codes, export license lists, and enforcement schedules.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:02.900
In practice, each side maintains a running list of disputed items.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.080
When the lists are frozen rather than expanded, the truce holds.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.480
The last three US China pauses followed the same pattern. Treasury and Commerce teams first

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:19.100
reconciled customs data, then political principles announced the result. Knowing this,

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:23.880
This, when you hear claims that one leader won the extension, you can check whether the underlying

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.980
lists actually stayed frozen or merely paused.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:32.400
The concrete detail worth watching is whether the January deadline produces new terror

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.860
filings or another technical freeze.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:41.300
Officials on both sides track thousands of individual product lines, and any mismatch in those

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.480
codes can reopen disputes overnight.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:50.620
Historical pauses show that the real work happens in spreadsheets exchanged between agencies rather than in

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.180
summit rooms. When the lists remain unchanged, companies gain the predictability they need for

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:02.360
shipping schedules. Readers can verify progress by watching the next round of US customs data releases

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:07.860
for any sudden additions to tariff lists. If you want to go deeper on the trade truce,

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.680
compare how Nikkei Asia and Al Jazeera are covering it.

